<article class="env-definition" id="083Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/083Q">Definition <span data-tag="083Q">67.13.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : Y \to X$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $Z \subset X$ be a closed subspace. The <em>inverse image $f^{-1}(Z)$ of the closed subspace $Z$</em> is the closed subspace $Z \times _ X Y$ of $Y$. </p>
